d compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["NVR, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $16.0B market cap on $10.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","The business throws off $1.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.84\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 60\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 11.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 5.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $8.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-8533856.37},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preference